WEBVTT

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.137
Last time, on Star Trek:
The Next Generation...

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.072
We will have to move quickly,
if we are to be successful.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.132
Successful?

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.642
Yes.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.737
In preventing
a Klingon civil war.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.111
I would speak with you.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.912
I do not hear
the words of traitors.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:21.443
It was Duras' father
who betrayed our people

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.457
to the Romulans at Khitomer,
not mine.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.392
We have discovered
that our brother

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.157
did, indeed, have
a son and heir.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.290
Follow me, and I
will show you honor.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.564
Your blood will paint the way
to the future.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.997
If we go to the aid
of the Bortas

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.976
we'll be dragging the Federation
into a Klingon civil war.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.536
You both fought as warriors.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.378
I return your family honor.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.941
Mr. Worf,
your responsibilities

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.919
as a Starfleet officer
are incompatible

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.818
with remaining
onboard a Klingon ship

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.152
during a time of war.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:02.355
Then I resign my commission
as a Starfleet officer.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.061
Picard has rejected
Gowron's plea for help.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.729
The Enterprise has left orbit.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.573
We should not discount
Jean-Luc Picard yet.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.599
He is human

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.306
and humans have a way
of showing up

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.644
when you least expect them.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.014
And now, the conclusion.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.586
Maintain course.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.922
Status of warp engines.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.393
Warp engines at 60%.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.692
Status of shields.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.391
Aft shields buckling.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.404
Transfer auxiliary power

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.962
to shields.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.640
Aft shields are gone.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.414
We cannot win.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.179
We must withdraw.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.813
Keep your place.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.454
New course.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.828
307 mark 275.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.959
But, sir, that takes us
dangerously close to...

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.059
GhoS!

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.238
We are entering
the star's corona.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.644
We will reach the photosphere
in 30 seconds.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.481
Stand by to enter warp
on my command.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.215
Set course 250

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.587
mark 015.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.819
Shields failing.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.521
Outer hull temperature
exceeding design limit.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.862
Captain!

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:49.391
Maintain course.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.003
They're closing on us.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.373
Stand by.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.976
DaH!

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:31.636
Captain's Log, Stardate 45020.4.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.873
We have arrived at Starbase 234

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.608
where I've taken the opportunity

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.980
to make a proposal
to Fleet Admiral Shanthi.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.349
There have been
three major engagements

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.684
in the past two weeks,
all of them won

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.815
by ships Ioyal
to the Duras family.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.587
None of which
is our concern, Jean-Luc.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.460
The Klingon civil war is,
by definition

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.828
an internal matter
of the Empire.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.093
Agreed.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.125
But if the Duras are being aided
by the Romulans

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.933
it becomes very much
our concern.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.997
The Romulans have been
attempting to destroy

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.803
the Klingon/Federation
Alliance

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.139
for the past 20 years.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.838
And at the same time

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.369
the Duras have been secretly
conspiring with the Romulans.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.041
Doesn't it strike you as odd

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.847
that the Duras are able to field
such an overpowering force

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.648
against Gowron
that they outmatch him

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.711
at almost every turn?

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.814
Some would call it
good leadership.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.122
And some would say that
they must be getting help.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.424
The Romulans are prepared
to take enormous risks

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:26.489
to gain any advantage
over the Federation.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.501
Can we seriously believe
that now, with the future

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.696
of the Klingon Empire
in the balance

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:33.672
they're content
to stand by and watch?

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:38.666
What is it you propose, Captain?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.805
We must stop the flow
of supplies and equipment

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.907
to the Duras from the Romulans.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:48.314
What I propose
is that we send a fleet

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.549
to the Romulan/Klingon border.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:54.549
We take no offensive action,
but we will be in a position

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.494
to expose any Romulan supplies

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.554
that attempt to cross
the border.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:04:59.792
A blockade?

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.163
Exactly.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.728
But how will you overcome
the Romulan cloaking device?

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:08.798
My Chief Engineer
has developed a system

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.503
that should nullify
that advantage.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:15.071
Each ship will send out
an active tachyon beam

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.105
to the other blockading ships.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.618
Now, in theory
any cloaked vessel

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.678
that attempts to pass
between our ships

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:25.623
must cross that beam
and be detected.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:32.496
I'll have to clear this
with the Federation Council.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:36.662
In the meantime,
assemble your fleet, Captain.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:41.962
Nicely done.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:44.135
I hope we know what we're doing.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.667
So do I, Number One.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:17.408
Space, the final frontier.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:21.277
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:23.281
Its continuing mission...

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:27.251
to explore strange new worlds

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:31.723
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:36.285
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:07:32.517 --> 00:07:36.351
Captain's Log, Stardate 45021.3.

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:39.585
Convincing Starfleet Command
to establish a blockade

00:07:39.624 --> 00:07:41.148
was relatively painless.

00:07:41.192 --> 00:07:44.389
Implementing that plan
is proving more troublesome.

00:07:44.429 --> 00:07:45.589
Starfleet is stretched

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.961
pretty thin
across this quadrant.

00:07:47.031 --> 00:07:48.225
There are only about 12 ships

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:49.858
within a day's travel
of this position.

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.129
The only other ships available

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:52.636
are either in Spacedock
for repairs

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.103
or still under construction.

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.369
Most of them don't even
have full crews yet.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:59.172
We could probably scare up
seven, maybe eight more ships.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.507
Mr. La Forge, can you implement

00:08:00.545 --> 00:08:02.342
your tachyon detection grid
with 20 ships?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.438
It's possible.

00:08:03.481 --> 00:08:06.507
But the more ships,
the bigger the net we can throw.

00:08:06.551 --> 00:08:07.711
All right.

00:08:07.752 --> 00:08:09.720
I'm going to add the Tian An Men

00:08:09.754 --> 00:08:11.381
the Sutherland and the Hermes

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:13.914
whether the yard superintendent
says they're ready or not.

00:08:14.025 --> 00:08:15.583
Mr. Data, will you
select a group

00:08:15.627 --> 00:08:17.891
of experienced
Enterprise officers to augment

00:08:17.929 --> 00:08:19.157
the crews of those ships?

00:08:19.197 --> 00:08:20.391
Aye, sir.

00:08:20.432 --> 00:08:22.559
Will, I want you
to command the Excalibur.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.828
Her crew was reassigned

00:08:23.868 --> 00:08:25.392
when she put in for repairs.

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:27.598
Geordi, you will be
his First Officer.

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:28.799
Aye, sir.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.934
I want the fleet underway
by 0900 tomorrow.

00:08:32.043 --> 00:08:33.943
Thank you, gentlemen.

00:08:37.048 --> 00:08:39.073
Yes, Mr. Data?

00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:42.575
May I ask a question, sir,
of a personal nature?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.088
Yes.

00:08:45.123 --> 00:08:46.647
I am confused.

00:08:46.691 --> 00:08:48.420
Why have I not been assigned

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.724
to command a ship
in the fleet, sir?

00:08:53.064 --> 00:08:54.929
Well, I felt
that you would be needed here.

00:08:54.966 --> 00:08:56.331
Why do you ask?

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:59.200
You have commented on the lack
of senior officers

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:00.499
available for this mission.

00:09:00.538 --> 00:09:02.529
I believe my 26 years
of Starfleet service

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:04.542
qualifies me for such a post.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.204
However, if you do not feel
the time has arrived

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:09.042
for an android
to command a starship

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.514
perhaps I should address myself
to improving...

00:09:11.549 --> 00:09:13.881
Commander...

00:09:15.753 --> 00:09:18.051
I believe
the Starship Sutherland

00:09:18.089 --> 00:09:19.454
will need a Captain.

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:20.924
I can think of no one

00:09:20.992 --> 00:09:23.517
better suited
for that task than you.

00:09:23.561 --> 00:09:25.256
Thank you, sir.

00:09:58.296 --> 00:10:02.062
You always did have fools
working for you, Larg.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.261
Now you don't have as many.

00:10:04.302 --> 00:10:05.599
Hey, you were lucky, Kurn

00:10:05.637 --> 00:10:07.264
but luck always runs out.

00:10:07.305 --> 00:10:10.138
Someday I will stand
over your broken corpse

00:10:10.174 --> 00:10:12.608
and drink to the victory
of the Duras.

00:10:14.178 --> 00:10:16.373
Ah, Worf...
Worf, good.

00:10:16.414 --> 00:10:19.383
This piece of baktag
is Captain Larg.

00:10:19.417 --> 00:10:21.510
He commanded the squadron

00:10:21.553 --> 00:10:24.386
that tried to destroy us
yesterday.

00:10:24.422 --> 00:10:26.982
Ah, the infamous Worf,
son of Mogh.

00:10:27.058 --> 00:10:29.288
What is that you are wearing?

00:10:29.327 --> 00:10:31.887
That is the uniform
of a Klingon!

00:10:33.164 --> 00:10:35.359
The Capital City
is neutral ground

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.630
and Larg's men are all around us

00:10:37.669 --> 00:10:38.727
as are mine.

00:10:40.004 --> 00:10:42.302
Good to drink with you, Kurn.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.399
May you die well.

00:10:44.442 --> 00:10:46.342
Die well, Larg.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.758
You drink with our enemies?

00:11:00.792 --> 00:11:02.692
How many are Gowron's men?

00:11:02.727 --> 00:11:05.958
How many are Duras'?

00:11:06.064 --> 00:11:07.964
Does it matter?

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:10.763
When we meet in battle,
we will fight to the death

00:11:10.802 --> 00:11:12.360
but here...
here, we're all warriors

00:11:12.403 --> 00:11:13.893
all Klingons.

00:11:13.938 --> 00:11:16.805
The repairs to the
Hegh'ta are proceeding.

00:11:16.841 --> 00:11:18.468
The port stabilizers...

00:11:18.509 --> 00:11:21.376
Is there nothing
in your heart but duty?

00:11:21.412 --> 00:11:23.380
It is my responsibility.

00:11:23.414 --> 00:11:26.542
We all have
responsibilities and duties

00:11:26.584 --> 00:11:30.111
but you and I are warriors
fighting in a great war.

00:11:30.154 --> 00:11:31.678
Think of it.

00:11:31.723 --> 00:11:35.750
You and I will fight battles
that others can only dream of.

00:11:35.793 --> 00:11:37.818
The time for glory is here.

00:11:37.862 --> 00:11:41.263
It is not a time
to worry about stabilizers.

00:11:41.299 --> 00:11:43.733
It is a time to celebrate

00:11:43.768 --> 00:11:46.430
for tomorrow we all may die!

00:11:48.506 --> 00:11:50.997
Come, let us, the sons of Mogh

00:11:51.109 --> 00:11:53.634
live this night
as if it were our last.

00:11:53.678 --> 00:11:55.578
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:12:04.956 --> 00:12:07.584
Worf is not like his brother.

00:12:07.625 --> 00:12:08.922
No.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.393
He tries to be

00:12:10.428 --> 00:12:12.919
but he's still
unsure of himself.

00:12:12.964 --> 00:12:17.094
Perhaps he needs something
to help restore his confidence.

00:12:17.135 --> 00:12:20.263
I think he'll find
our offer appealing.

00:12:20.304 --> 00:12:23.296
I'll make sure he does.

00:12:33.651 --> 00:12:36.119
You've got to keep
this mixture above 90%

00:12:36.154 --> 00:12:38.315
or we'll never leave orbit.

00:12:39.724 --> 00:12:41.817
Thank you, Mr. Craig.

00:12:46.998 --> 00:12:49.466
I am Lieutenant Commander Data.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.934
Lieutenant Commander
Christopher Hobson.

00:12:51.969 --> 00:12:53.368
By order of Starfleet

00:12:53.404 --> 00:12:55.770
I hereby take command
of this vessel.

00:12:55.807 --> 00:12:57.297
Please note the time and date

00:12:57.341 --> 00:12:58.933
in the ship's log.

00:13:01.112 --> 00:13:02.739
Excuse me, sir.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:06.272
I'd like to request a transfer.

00:13:06.317 --> 00:13:08.877
May I ask why?

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:13.948
I don't believe I'd be
a good First Officer for you.

00:13:14.058 --> 00:13:15.787
Your service record to date
suggests

00:13:15.827 --> 00:13:17.920
you would perform
that function adequately.

00:13:17.962 --> 00:13:19.088
No, no, no.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:20.757
That's not what I mean.

00:13:20.798 --> 00:13:24.359
I don't think I'd be
a good First Officer for you.

00:13:24.402 --> 00:13:26.461
Why?

00:13:26.504 --> 00:13:28.096
Frankly, sir, I don't believe

00:13:28.139 --> 00:13:30.232
in your ability
to command this ship.

00:13:30.274 --> 00:13:32.970
You're a fellow officer,
and I respect that

00:13:33.044 --> 00:13:34.602
but no one would suggest

00:13:34.645 --> 00:13:37.739
that a Klingon would be
a good ship's counselor

00:13:37.782 --> 00:13:39.716
or that a Berellian
could be an engineer.

00:13:39.751 --> 00:13:41.878
They're just not suited
for those positions.

00:13:41.919 --> 00:13:45.150
By the same token,
I don't think an android

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:47.657
is a good choice to be Captain.

00:13:50.995 --> 00:13:52.963
I understand your concerns.

00:13:52.997 --> 00:13:54.931
Request denied.

00:14:00.671 --> 00:14:02.662
The Endeavor has cleared
the dock, Captain.

00:14:02.707 --> 00:14:03.901
All ships standing by.

00:14:03.941 --> 00:14:05.067
Good.

00:14:05.109 --> 00:14:07.407
Course 118 mark 357,
full impulse power.

00:14:07.445 --> 00:14:10.141
Signal the fleet
to get underway.

00:14:10.181 --> 00:14:12.741
We'll enter warp once
we're clear of the system.

00:14:12.784 --> 00:14:14.115
Aye, sir.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.921
Engage.

00:14:34.837 --> 00:14:37.135
The Romulan convoy is late.

00:14:37.173 --> 00:14:39.198
We need those supplies.

00:14:39.242 --> 00:14:42.973
Gowron has suffered another loss
near the Mempa system.

00:14:43.012 --> 00:14:46.311
His forces will not threaten you
in that region for some time.

00:14:46.349 --> 00:14:47.441
But if Gowron...

00:14:47.483 --> 00:14:49.644
The convoy will arrive
in due course.

00:14:49.686 --> 00:14:52.246
A Federation fleet
has left Starbase 234.

00:14:52.288 --> 00:14:54.916
They've set course
for Klingon territory.

00:14:54.958 --> 00:14:56.084
How many?

00:14:56.125 --> 00:14:57.422
At least 20 starships.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.757
Who is commanding this fleet?

00:14:58.795 --> 00:14:59.762
Picard.

00:14:59.796 --> 00:15:01.024
What does it mean?

00:15:01.064 --> 00:15:03.362
Is the Federation
going to enter the war?

00:15:03.399 --> 00:15:05.264
Should we attack them
before they get here?

00:15:05.301 --> 00:15:07.599
Silence the child,
or send him away.

00:15:07.637 --> 00:15:09.298
Movar.

00:15:11.074 --> 00:15:13.474
I want you to return
to Romulus immediately.

00:15:13.509 --> 00:15:15.340
Have all available ships
rendezvous

00:15:15.378 --> 00:15:17.107
at these coordinates
in two days.

00:15:17.146 --> 00:15:19.273
Yes, Commander.

00:15:19.315 --> 00:15:22.773
20 starships aren't enough
to wage war.

00:15:22.819 --> 00:15:25.287
Starfleet must be bluffing.

00:15:25.321 --> 00:15:26.982
Perhaps.

00:15:31.561 --> 00:15:35.122
Our forces in the Mempa sector
are now in full retreat.

00:15:35.164 --> 00:15:38.622
They will need to regroup
near Beta Lankal.

00:15:38.668 --> 00:15:42.604
We destroyed their supply bases
in that sector three weeks ago.

00:15:42.638 --> 00:15:44.799
How can they continue to fight?

00:15:44.841 --> 00:15:46.809
They must be getting help.

00:15:46.843 --> 00:15:49.539
Maybe they have better leaders.

00:15:58.821 --> 00:16:02.917
I say you have failed
as our leader, Gowron.

00:16:10.533 --> 00:16:12.433
There is no time for this.

00:16:12.468 --> 00:16:13.594
We must make plans

00:16:13.636 --> 00:16:16.036
before those forces
reach Beta Lankal.

00:16:16.072 --> 00:16:17.835
How can we oppose the Duras

00:16:17.874 --> 00:16:19.774
when we continue to fight
amongst ourselves?

00:16:19.809 --> 00:16:21.936
Gowron must answer
this challenge to his authority.

00:16:21.978 --> 00:16:23.240
Stop it!

00:16:23.279 --> 00:16:25.941
Do we fall upon ourselves
like a pack of Ferengi?!

00:16:25.982 --> 00:16:28.507
The enemy is the Duras!

00:16:28.551 --> 00:16:30.314
We are at war.

00:16:48.004 --> 00:16:52.668
Now the war... can continue.

00:16:58.281 --> 00:17:00.749
We're crossing into
Klingon territory, Captain.

00:17:00.783 --> 00:17:02.045
Signal the fleet to maintain

00:17:02.085 --> 00:17:03.746
Yellow Alert
until further notice.

00:17:03.786 --> 00:17:05.083
Aye, sir.

00:17:05.121 --> 00:17:07.112
Begin long-range scans
of the Romulan border.

00:17:08.524 --> 00:17:10.617
No uncloaked ships
within sensor range.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:13.060
A few subspace anomalies,
but nothing firm.

00:17:13.096 --> 00:17:15.587
Those anomalies
could be cloaked ships.

00:17:15.631 --> 00:17:17.929
Could be, sir.

00:17:17.967 --> 00:17:20.435
Open a channel to the Excalibur.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.438
Excalibur, Riker here.

00:17:22.472 --> 00:17:24.599
Deploy the fleet, Will.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.767
It's time to spread our net.

00:17:26.809 --> 00:17:27.901
Yes, sir.

00:17:32.615 --> 00:17:35.049
We've arrived at the designated
coordinates, Captain.

00:17:35.084 --> 00:17:36.915
All stop.
Notify the flagship

00:17:36.953 --> 00:17:38.784
that we have assumed station.

00:17:40.323 --> 00:17:42.621
Starboard power
coupling is overloaded.

00:17:42.658 --> 00:17:45.957
We've got a radiation leak
on decks 10 through 12.

00:17:45.995 --> 00:17:47.622
Why are the backups
not functioning?

00:17:47.663 --> 00:17:48.687
There wasn't enough time

00:17:48.731 --> 00:17:50.858
to test all the backups
before we left the yard.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.061
Terry, I want you
down in Engineering

00:17:53.102 --> 00:17:54.797
working on a new coupling.

00:17:54.837 --> 00:17:56.668
You have taken
the phaser and torpedo

00:17:56.706 --> 00:17:57.900
control units off-line.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.908
Keith, you and I will
start bringing rad...

00:17:59.942 --> 00:18:01.409
Mr. Hobson, it is inappropriate

00:18:01.444 --> 00:18:03.378
for you to determine
a course of action

00:18:03.412 --> 00:18:06.006
without consulting
your commanding officer.

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:09.017
I was trying to safeguard

00:18:09.051 --> 00:18:11.019
the lives of people
on those decks.

00:18:11.053 --> 00:18:12.748
But you're right.

00:18:12.788 --> 00:18:15.916
Belay those orders, everyone.

00:18:15.958 --> 00:18:19.621
Phasers and torpedoes
are back on-line.

00:18:21.964 --> 00:18:24.398
What should we do, sir?

00:18:24.433 --> 00:18:27.527
You will take the phaser
and torpedo units off-line

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.630
and begin repairs of
the starboard power coupling.

00:18:30.673 --> 00:18:33.267
Thank you, sir.

00:18:33.309 --> 00:18:35.300
You heard the Captain, everyone.

00:18:45.788 --> 00:18:47.312
We're ready, sir.

00:18:47.356 --> 00:18:49.119
Mr. La Forge,
how long do you think

00:18:49.158 --> 00:18:50.853
it will take the Romulans
to detect

00:18:50.893 --> 00:18:52.884
the tachyon field,
once it's activated?

00:18:52.929 --> 00:18:54.226
Not long.

00:18:54.263 --> 00:18:55.821
Romulan sensors
are as good as ours.

00:18:55.865 --> 00:18:58.231
Very well.

00:18:58.267 --> 00:18:59.791
Energize the network.

00:19:07.176 --> 00:19:09.701
Commander, there's an increase

00:19:09.745 --> 00:19:13.203
in tachyon emissions
from the Federation fleet.

00:19:15.751 --> 00:19:19.482
They're using the beams
as a detection field.

00:19:19.522 --> 00:19:22.582
If we try to cross it,
they'll see us

00:19:22.625 --> 00:19:24.593
even if we're cloaked.

00:19:24.627 --> 00:19:26.060
Issues orders to begin work

00:19:26.095 --> 00:19:27.926
on a way to penetrate
this field.

00:19:27.964 --> 00:19:29.625
In the meantime

00:19:29.665 --> 00:19:32.293
we'll have to convince
Captain Picard he should leave.

00:19:33.569 --> 00:19:36.800
Captain, I'm picking up
something directly ahead.

00:19:36.839 --> 00:19:39.000
Romulan ship decloaking.

00:19:42.545 --> 00:19:44.274
Shall I raise shields?

00:19:44.313 --> 00:19:45.575
Not yet.

00:19:45.615 --> 00:19:48.175
They're hailing us, sir.

00:19:48.217 --> 00:19:50.242
On screen.

00:19:58.494 --> 00:19:59.586
Tasha.

00:19:59.629 --> 00:20:01.494
No, Captain.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:04.966
My name is Commander Sela.

00:20:05.001 --> 00:20:09.961
The woman you knew as Tasha Yar
was my mother.

00:20:15.743 --> 00:20:18.541
Deploying an invasion fleet
along our border

00:20:18.579 --> 00:20:20.809
is a clear act
of aggression, Captain.

00:20:20.848 --> 00:20:22.372
It will not be tolerated.

00:20:22.416 --> 00:20:24.748
You have 20 hours
to recall your ships

00:20:24.785 --> 00:20:27.151
and return peacefully
to Federation territory.

00:20:34.795 --> 00:20:36.922
So, you believe her, Counselor?

00:20:36.964 --> 00:20:40.263
I'm not saying we should accept
her claim at face value

00:20:40.301 --> 00:20:42.394
but I sensed no deception
from her.

00:20:42.436 --> 00:20:45.564
She really believes
she's the daughter of Tasha Yar.

00:20:45.606 --> 00:20:47.005
Regardless
of what she believes

00:20:47.108 --> 00:20:48.405
Sela can't be her daughter.

00:20:48.442 --> 00:20:50.603
I've reviewed all
of Tasha's medical records

00:20:50.645 --> 00:20:53.239
and there is no indication
that she was ever pregnant.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:56.147
Besides, Tasha was a child
when this woman was born.

00:20:56.183 --> 00:20:57.878
Sela could have been cloned.

00:20:57.918 --> 00:21:00.011
Or had her appearance
surgically altered.

00:21:00.087 --> 00:21:01.520
But why?

00:21:01.555 --> 00:21:04.888
What possible advantage
could there be to the Romulans?

00:21:04.925 --> 00:21:06.552
As this now stands,
I don't think

00:21:06.594 --> 00:21:09.119
this will have any impact
on our present strategy.

00:21:09.163 --> 00:21:10.596
We'll continue the blockade.

00:21:10.631 --> 00:21:12.826
Leave the next move to them.
Thank you.

00:21:22.476 --> 00:21:24.444
Am I intruding?

00:21:24.478 --> 00:21:26.105
No, not at all.

00:21:26.147 --> 00:21:28.911
Is something wrong?

00:21:28.949 --> 00:21:30.576
News travels fast.

00:21:30.618 --> 00:21:33.086
I heard
that Tasha Yar's daughter

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.452
is aboard the Romulan ship.

00:21:36.991 --> 00:21:38.481
I think that the Romulans

00:21:38.526 --> 00:21:40.892
are just hoping
to create a distraction.

00:21:40.928 --> 00:21:43.624
They want to keep us
off-balance.

00:21:43.664 --> 00:21:45.427
Hmm.

00:21:45.466 --> 00:21:48.230
How much do you know
about what happened

00:21:48.269 --> 00:21:50.669
to the last ship
called Enterprise?

00:21:50.705 --> 00:21:52.332
The Enterprise-C?

00:21:52.373 --> 00:21:55.274
It was lost
at the Battle of Narendra III

00:21:55.309 --> 00:21:58.210
defending a Klingon outpost
from the Romulans.

00:21:58.245 --> 00:22:00.270
And the survivors?

00:22:00.314 --> 00:22:04.273
There were stories of prisoners
taken back to Romulus

00:22:04.318 --> 00:22:06.650
but these were only rumors.

00:22:08.556 --> 00:22:09.887
No.

00:22:09.924 --> 00:22:12.222
There were survivors.

00:22:12.259 --> 00:22:14.921
And Tasha Yar was one of them.

00:22:14.962 --> 00:22:18.557
Guinan, that was 23 years ago.

00:22:18.599 --> 00:22:21.159
Tasha Yar was only a child.

00:22:21.202 --> 00:22:22.726
I know that.

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:26.900
But I also know
she was aboard that ship

00:22:26.941 --> 00:22:29.409
and she was not a child.

00:22:29.443 --> 00:22:31.411
And I think...

00:22:31.445 --> 00:22:33.345
you sent her there.

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:36.213
How can that be?

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:37.979
I don't know.

00:22:38.085 --> 00:22:40.519
I just know that you did.

00:22:40.554 --> 00:22:42.920
Tasha died...

00:22:42.957 --> 00:22:45.949
a year before you came
on the Enterprise.

00:22:45.993 --> 00:22:47.620
You never met her.

00:22:47.661 --> 00:22:49.288
I know that.

00:22:51.699 --> 00:22:53.997
If you have only
a vague intuition...

00:22:54.068 --> 00:22:56.366
You can't just dismiss this.

00:22:56.403 --> 00:22:58.200
If I'm right

00:22:58.239 --> 00:23:01.936
then you are responsible
for this whole situation.

00:23:03.744 --> 00:23:07.942
I think it's time
that I met Commander Sela.

00:23:14.555 --> 00:23:16.182
We are at war.

00:23:16.223 --> 00:23:18.453
Gowron should forbid
any challenges

00:23:18.492 --> 00:23:20.187
until we are victorious.

00:23:20.227 --> 00:23:22.661
A Klingon does not postpone
a matter of honor.

00:23:22.696 --> 00:23:24.823
A Klingon should place
the good of the Empire

00:23:24.865 --> 00:23:26.457
above his own pride.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.627
Oh, so now, Gowron
no longer suits you.

00:23:28.669 --> 00:23:30.466
Perhaps you wish
to challenge him

00:23:30.504 --> 00:23:32.369
for the leadership
of the Council.

00:23:32.406 --> 00:23:33.373
No!

00:23:33.407 --> 00:23:35.136
Then do not speak of this again.

00:23:35.176 --> 00:23:37.542
I did not wish to follow Gowron.

00:23:37.578 --> 00:23:41.674
You came to me and insisted
that we support Gowron

00:23:41.715 --> 00:23:43.808
against the Duras family.

00:23:43.851 --> 00:23:46.479
The time for debate is over.

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:48.147
We are Klingons.

00:23:48.189 --> 00:23:49.747
He is our leader.

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:51.280
If that is not enough for you

00:23:51.325 --> 00:23:53.316
then perhaps you made
the wrong choice

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:56.727
when you put on that uniform.

00:24:27.827 --> 00:24:29.795
Well, Captain

00:24:29.829 --> 00:24:32.923
what is this urgent matter
we need to discuss?

00:24:32.966 --> 00:24:34.957
Please, won't you sit down?

00:24:38.738 --> 00:24:40.638
I'm afraid that
you have misinterpreted

00:24:40.673 --> 00:24:42.436
our presence here.

00:24:42.475 --> 00:24:45.967
I want to reassure you that
we have no hostile intention.

00:24:46.079 --> 00:24:48.604
Ah.

00:24:48.648 --> 00:24:51.276
So then, I can tell my superiors

00:24:51.317 --> 00:24:54.286
that a fleet
of 23 Federation starships

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:56.948
is on our border for... what?

00:24:56.990 --> 00:24:58.855
Humanitarian reasons?

00:24:58.892 --> 00:25:02.328
It is our intent
to prevent any external power

00:25:02.362 --> 00:25:05.024
from interfering
in Klingon affairs.

00:25:05.064 --> 00:25:07.931
Nor do we have
any plan to do so.

00:25:08.001 --> 00:25:10.231
But, Captain, if for any reason

00:25:10.270 --> 00:25:12.830
we chose to enter
Klingon territory

00:25:12.872 --> 00:25:14.499
how would you stop us?

00:25:14.541 --> 00:25:18.068
With our cloaking devices,
we can slip by you at will.

00:25:18.111 --> 00:25:20.875
Then why don't you
just take your ships across?

00:25:23.183 --> 00:25:25.651
You sound eager for us to try.

00:25:25.685 --> 00:25:29.519
Perhaps you've discovered
a method in detecting our ships?

00:25:32.025 --> 00:25:35.324
However, I don't think
you asked me here

00:25:35.361 --> 00:25:38.159
to discuss
our military situation.

00:25:38.198 --> 00:25:39.165
All right.

00:25:39.199 --> 00:25:41.224
Why did I invite you here?

00:25:42.502 --> 00:25:45.835
You want the answer to
the only question on your mind.

00:25:45.872 --> 00:25:48.636
How could Tasha Yar
be my mother?

00:25:48.675 --> 00:25:49.937
It's been suggested

00:25:49.976 --> 00:25:52.342
that she was on board
the Enterprise-C

00:25:52.378 --> 00:25:54.539
when it was destroyed
24 years ago

00:25:54.581 --> 00:25:56.674
that she was
one of the survivors

00:25:56.716 --> 00:25:58.741
and that, obviously,
you are a product

00:25:58.785 --> 00:26:00.946
of a union
between her and a Romulan.

00:26:02.388 --> 00:26:05.255
But you know that's impossible.

00:26:05.291 --> 00:26:07.919
She would have been a child
when that battle occurred.

00:26:07.961 --> 00:26:09.929
But you claim
that it is possible...

00:26:09.963 --> 00:26:12.193
that you're the daughter
of Tasha Yar.

00:26:16.669 --> 00:26:20.628
Yes, she was on that ship
24 years ago.

00:26:20.673 --> 00:26:25.736
She was sent there
by you from the future.

00:26:34.153 --> 00:26:36.951
She was among those
few who survived.

00:26:37.023 --> 00:26:38.854
They were all
to have been executed

00:26:38.892 --> 00:26:40.154
after the interrogation

00:26:40.193 --> 00:26:43.959
but a Romulan general saw her
and became enamored with her.

00:26:43.997 --> 00:26:45.487
So a deal was struck.

00:26:45.532 --> 00:26:47.523
Their lives would be spared

00:26:47.567 --> 00:26:49.432
if she became his consort.

00:26:51.204 --> 00:26:53.001
I was born a year later.

00:26:55.308 --> 00:26:57.435
I want to meet your mother.

00:26:57.477 --> 00:26:59.206
Can you arrange that?

00:27:02.315 --> 00:27:05.807
One night, when I was
four years old, she came to me.

00:27:05.852 --> 00:27:07.547
She bundled me up,
and she told me

00:27:07.587 --> 00:27:10.112
to stay quiet
as we left the compound.

00:27:11.558 --> 00:27:13.924
Well, I realized
she was taking me away.

00:27:13.993 --> 00:27:16.894
She was taking me away
from my home, my father.

00:27:16.930 --> 00:27:18.227
So I cried out.

00:27:18.264 --> 00:27:20.289
My father offered her life.

00:27:20.333 --> 00:27:21.766
He gave her a home.

00:27:21.801 --> 00:27:23.234
He gave her a child.

00:27:23.269 --> 00:27:25.294
And how did she repay him?

00:27:25.338 --> 00:27:26.999
By betrayal.

00:27:29.008 --> 00:27:30.999
They executed her.

00:27:39.319 --> 00:27:43.813
Everything in me that was human
died that day with my mother.

00:27:43.856 --> 00:27:46.086
All that's left now is Romulan.

00:27:46.125 --> 00:27:48.218
Never doubt that.

00:27:48.261 --> 00:27:50.252
Doubts?

00:27:50.296 --> 00:27:52.287
I'm full of them.

00:27:55.301 --> 00:27:58.134
But nothing in my experience
can persuade me

00:27:58.171 --> 00:28:00.298
that what you have told me
is true.

00:28:00.340 --> 00:28:01.898
And I do know one thing...

00:28:01.975 --> 00:28:05.570
it will not affect my judgment
at our next encounter.

00:28:07.146 --> 00:28:09.614
You have 14 hours, Captain.

00:28:09.649 --> 00:28:13.244
I suggest you use them wisely.

00:28:42.915 --> 00:28:44.815
Something wrong?

00:28:44.851 --> 00:28:47.547
Welcome, Worf, son of Mogh.

00:28:48.655 --> 00:28:49.713
What do you want?

00:28:49.756 --> 00:28:51.053
The same as you.

00:28:51.090 --> 00:28:54.582
Personal honor,
glory for the Empire.

00:28:54.627 --> 00:28:58.222
Your family
has never valued honor.

00:28:58.264 --> 00:29:00.255
You only knew our brother.

00:29:00.299 --> 00:29:01.891
We are not like him.

00:29:01.968 --> 00:29:04.903
Our brother made many mistakes.

00:29:04.971 --> 00:29:08.270
One was to make you an enemy.

00:29:08.307 --> 00:29:10.605
We would rather be your friends.

00:29:10.643 --> 00:29:13.271
Then you should not
have opposed Gowron.

00:29:13.312 --> 00:29:14.904
Oh, Gowron is nothing.

00:29:14.981 --> 00:29:17.541
Toral is Duras' only son

00:29:17.583 --> 00:29:21.610
and he will be the leader
of the Council.

00:29:21.654 --> 00:29:23.918
In your heart,
even you know that.

00:29:23.990 --> 00:29:25.924
But Toral needs guidance.

00:29:25.992 --> 00:29:28.119
A firm hand.

00:29:28.161 --> 00:29:30.288
A father figure.

00:29:30.329 --> 00:29:32.923
That could be you

00:29:32.999 --> 00:29:36.298
if you were mated to B'Etor.

00:29:36.335 --> 00:29:39.395
The rewards could be greater
than you can imagine.

00:29:39.439 --> 00:29:41.532
Nothing would stand in our way.

00:29:41.574 --> 00:29:44.805
We could rule the Empire
together.

00:29:44.844 --> 00:29:48.041
Join us, Worf,
and usher in a new era

00:29:48.081 --> 00:29:49.480
for our people.

00:29:49.515 --> 00:29:52.348
An era where honor
has no meaning?

00:29:55.421 --> 00:29:58.515
Where Klingons trade Ioyalties
in dark rooms

00:29:58.558 --> 00:30:01.857
and the Empire is ruled
from Romulus.

00:30:04.030 --> 00:30:05.964
Enough, Lursa.

00:30:06.032 --> 00:30:07.693
You've failed.

00:30:07.734 --> 00:30:09.759
I need to know
the strength and capabilities

00:30:09.802 --> 00:30:10.928
of the Federation fleet.

00:30:10.970 --> 00:30:12.528
I don't have time for this.

00:30:12.572 --> 00:30:14.130
Turn him over to the guard.

00:30:14.173 --> 00:30:16.835
B'Etor can have him back
when they've finished with him.

00:30:17.543 --> 00:30:18.532
Come!

00:30:25.985 --> 00:30:27.577
In 13 hours, we'll be forced

00:30:27.620 --> 00:30:29.588
to either withdraw
from the border

00:30:29.622 --> 00:30:31.419
or fight the Romulan fleet.

00:30:31.457 --> 00:30:33.721
Neither alternative
is acceptable.

00:30:33.760 --> 00:30:37.252
We must expose their involvement
before the deadline.

00:30:37.296 --> 00:30:38.854
What is it you propose?

00:30:38.898 --> 00:30:41.298
If you launch
a full-scale attack now

00:30:41.334 --> 00:30:44.201
then the Duras fleet
will call for supplies.

00:30:44.237 --> 00:30:46.535
Lursa and B'Etor
will call for help.

00:30:46.572 --> 00:30:48.870
The Romulans will try
to run the blockade

00:30:48.908 --> 00:30:50.876
and we'll be ready for them.

00:30:50.910 --> 00:30:55.006
And once the Romulan connection
has been exposed

00:30:55.081 --> 00:30:58.983
support will fall away
from Lursa and B'Etor.

00:30:59.018 --> 00:31:00.178
Very well.

00:31:00.219 --> 00:31:03.245
I will make preparations.

00:31:03.289 --> 00:31:06.122
One thing more, Picard.

00:31:06.159 --> 00:31:10.653
Worf has been captured
by the Duras.

00:31:10.696 --> 00:31:13.494
I hope he dies well.

00:31:13.533 --> 00:31:16.001
Qapla'!

00:31:23.442 --> 00:31:26.536
When Gowron begins his attack,
then we will make our move.

00:31:26.578 --> 00:31:29.138
Excalibur will fall back
with engine problems.

00:31:29.181 --> 00:31:32.241
And you will take the Akagi
and the Hornet to this position

00:31:32.284 --> 00:31:34.479
which will open a small gap
in our detection net.

00:31:34.519 --> 00:31:35.486
And if the Romulans

00:31:35.520 --> 00:31:37.215
are already aware
of the tachyon field

00:31:37.255 --> 00:31:39.223
they should run
the blockade at that point.

00:31:39.257 --> 00:31:41.282
Exactly. But when they try
to bring their ships through

00:31:41.326 --> 00:31:42.657
the Enterprise
and the Tian An Men

00:31:42.694 --> 00:31:45.788
will swing around,
close the gap...

00:31:45.831 --> 00:31:47.890
and catch them in the act.

00:31:49.835 --> 00:31:51.302
Very nice.

00:31:51.336 --> 00:31:53.327
I'd better get back.

00:31:55.841 --> 00:31:57.172
Good luck, Will.

00:31:57.209 --> 00:31:58.699
Good luck, Captain.

00:32:10.022 --> 00:32:12.354
We've just received
an urgent message

00:32:12.391 --> 00:32:13.756
from Lursa and B'Etor.

00:32:13.792 --> 00:32:16.283
Gowron's forces have attacked
in three sectors.

00:32:16.328 --> 00:32:18.819
The Duras are nearing defeat.

00:32:18.864 --> 00:32:20.593
You mean, they were caught
unprepared

00:32:20.632 --> 00:32:22.156
and now they're crying for help.

00:32:25.337 --> 00:32:27.237
Have the science sections
found a way

00:32:27.272 --> 00:32:29.331
to circumvent
the detection grid yet?

00:32:29.374 --> 00:32:30.864
We think so.

00:32:34.479 --> 00:32:35.946
Just before we cross the border

00:32:35.981 --> 00:32:37.881
we'll send out
a massive tachyon pulse.

00:32:37.916 --> 00:32:40.783
A burst that large should cause

00:32:40.819 --> 00:32:44.949
enough interference to disable
a part of their network.

00:32:44.990 --> 00:32:46.480
Good.

00:32:46.525 --> 00:32:50.086
One of their ships
is moving off the blockade line.

00:32:50.128 --> 00:32:51.891
Their warp drive is failing.

00:32:51.930 --> 00:32:53.261
Picard is redeploying the fleet

00:32:53.298 --> 00:32:55.994
to compensate
for the missing ship.

00:32:56.034 --> 00:32:57.865
There's a gap opening
in the net.

00:32:57.903 --> 00:33:00.701
He doesn't have enough ships
to maintain the network.

00:33:00.739 --> 00:33:03.936
If we act quickly,
we can move through.

00:33:06.678 --> 00:33:08.441
Commander?!

00:33:08.480 --> 00:33:09.708
No.

00:33:09.748 --> 00:33:11.375
I don't think so.

00:33:11.416 --> 00:33:13.145
But it's what
we've been waiting for.

00:33:13.185 --> 00:33:14.152
Yes, I know

00:33:14.186 --> 00:33:16.279
and so does Picard.

00:33:16.321 --> 00:33:18.721
He's giving us
exactly what we need

00:33:18.757 --> 00:33:20.816
and he expects us to take it.

00:33:20.859 --> 00:33:23.953
No. We won't step
into Picard's trap.

00:33:23.995 --> 00:33:26.964
We will disable
part of his network...

00:33:26.998 --> 00:33:29.193
here, where they're weakest.

00:33:29.234 --> 00:33:31.668
We'll direct the energy burst

00:33:31.703 --> 00:33:35.366
right at the ship
with the android Captain.

00:33:40.378 --> 00:33:42.608
Sir, the detection net
is picking up

00:33:42.647 --> 00:33:44.308
activity from the Romulans.

00:33:44.349 --> 00:33:47.341
15 cloaked ships
spreading out along the border.

00:33:47.385 --> 00:33:49.114
Signal the fleet to stand by.

00:33:49.154 --> 00:33:50.519
Aye, sir.

00:33:51.790 --> 00:33:52.916
Now.

00:33:55.961 --> 00:33:59.897
Come to course 080 mark 295.

00:34:01.233 --> 00:34:04.066
There's a disruption
in the tachyon detectors.

00:34:09.741 --> 00:34:12.938
It's localized
to this segment of the net.

00:34:13.011 --> 00:34:15.377
Open a channel
to the Sutherland.

00:34:15.413 --> 00:34:17.040
Data here, sir.

00:34:17.082 --> 00:34:20.483
We're reading a disruption
of the tachyon net in your area.

00:34:20.519 --> 00:34:23.181
Yes, sir. The Romulans have
released a high-energy burst.

00:34:23.221 --> 00:34:24.950
The net is no longer effective
in a radius

00:34:25.056 --> 00:34:27.581
of 10 million kilometers
around the Sutherland.

00:34:27.626 --> 00:34:29.423
That's where
they're going through.

00:34:29.461 --> 00:34:30.792
Send a signal to the fleet.

00:34:30.829 --> 00:34:33.457
All ships to fall back
and rendezvous at Gamma Eridon.

00:34:33.498 --> 00:34:35.864
We'll reestablish the net there.

00:34:35.901 --> 00:34:37.562
Aye, sir.

00:34:43.408 --> 00:34:48.175
All Federation ships proceed
at maximum warp to Gamma Eridon.

00:34:48.213 --> 00:34:49.976
Acknowledge the signal.

00:34:50.048 --> 00:34:52.676
Ensign, lay in a course
and engage at warp 9.3.

00:34:52.717 --> 00:34:55.049
Aye, sir.

00:35:06.464 --> 00:35:07.931
What are you doing?

00:35:07.966 --> 00:35:10.935
In disrupting the detection net,
the Romulans may have caused

00:35:10.969 --> 00:35:14.200
a residual tachyon signature
to form around their own ships.

00:35:14.239 --> 00:35:16.400
But we have no way
of detecting it.

00:35:16.441 --> 00:35:18.068
All stop.

00:35:18.109 --> 00:35:20.407
Aye, sir. All stop.

00:35:22.247 --> 00:35:23.874
Sir...

00:35:23.915 --> 00:35:26.884
the fleet's been ordered
to Gamma Eridon.

00:35:26.918 --> 00:35:29.512
The tachyon signatures
will not last long.

00:35:29.554 --> 00:35:30.953
By the time the fleet
is deployed

00:35:31.056 --> 00:35:32.353
it will be too late.

00:35:32.390 --> 00:35:34.051
Begin to reconfigure the sensors

00:35:34.092 --> 00:35:35.923
to detect
ionized particle traces.

00:35:35.961 --> 00:35:38.794
The entire area's been flooded
with tachyon particles.

00:35:38.830 --> 00:35:41.492
We'll never be able to find
what we're looking for.

00:35:41.533 --> 00:35:43.160
I am aware of the difficulties.

00:35:43.201 --> 00:35:45.169
Please bring the phasers
back on line.

00:35:45.203 --> 00:35:47.899
That will flood three decks
with radiation.

00:35:47.939 --> 00:35:50.772
We will initiate radiation
protocol when necessary.

00:35:50.809 --> 00:35:52.709
You don't give a damn
about the people

00:35:52.744 --> 00:35:54.405
whose lives
you're throwing away.

00:35:54.446 --> 00:35:55.504
We're not just machines...

00:35:55.547 --> 00:35:57.174
Mr. Hobson!

00:35:57.215 --> 00:35:59.877
You will carry out my orders,
or I will relieve you of duty.

00:36:01.086 --> 00:36:02.747
Yes, sir.

00:36:08.927 --> 00:36:10.758
Captain, the Sutherland

00:36:10.795 --> 00:36:12.854
isn't heading
for the rendezvous point.

00:36:12.898 --> 00:36:14.923
She's come to a full stop.

00:36:15.033 --> 00:36:17.661
Open a channel.

00:36:19.337 --> 00:36:22.602
The Enterprise wants to know
the reason we've stopped.

00:36:22.641 --> 00:36:24.541
Display sensor schematic.

00:36:26.878 --> 00:36:29.938
Display sensor sweep,
maximum range.

00:36:31.449 --> 00:36:33.940
Are you going to answer
the Enterprise?

00:36:33.985 --> 00:36:37.216
Overlay display
with tachyon emissions.

00:36:40.558 --> 00:36:42.355
Highlight any tachyon signatures

00:36:42.394 --> 00:36:45.693
which show
subspace inertial displacement.

00:36:45.730 --> 00:36:48.665
Concentrate a sensor sweep
in that area.

00:36:48.700 --> 00:36:50.759
Sir, this is pointless.

00:36:50.802 --> 00:36:53.168
Those readings
could be anything.

00:36:53.204 --> 00:36:56.105
There's no way for us to be sure
the Romulans are out there.

00:36:56.141 --> 00:36:58.632
Reconfigure
photon torpedo warhead yields.

00:36:58.677 --> 00:37:01.145
Set for high-energy burst,
level six.

00:37:01.179 --> 00:37:02.646
Level six?
But that won't even...

00:37:02.681 --> 00:37:03.909
Do it!

00:37:07.385 --> 00:37:09.012
Torpedoes ready.

00:37:09.054 --> 00:37:11.352
Another message coming in.

00:37:11.389 --> 00:37:13.289
It's Captain Picard.

00:37:13.325 --> 00:37:16.226
Mr. Data, you were ordered
to rendezvous with the fleet

00:37:16.261 --> 00:37:17.853
at Gamma Eridon.

00:37:17.896 --> 00:37:19.056
Acknowledge.

00:37:19.097 --> 00:37:20.792
Stand by, Captain.

00:37:20.832 --> 00:37:22.459
Mr. Hobson, prepare to fire.

00:37:22.500 --> 00:37:24.024
Didn't you hear... Captain Picard

00:37:24.069 --> 00:37:25.730
- wants us...
- Fire.

00:37:27.339 --> 00:37:29.739
Fire!

00:37:39.250 --> 00:37:42.708
They have discovered us.

00:37:42.753 --> 00:37:44.118
Reverse course.

00:37:44.154 --> 00:37:46.486
Order the fleet back
to Romulan territory.

00:37:46.523 --> 00:37:49.549
Commander, the Duras
need this convoy.

00:37:49.593 --> 00:37:51.493
Without these supplies,
they cannot win.

00:37:51.528 --> 00:37:53.519
We've been discovered.
It's over.

00:37:53.564 --> 00:37:57.330
But what should I tell
Lursa and B'Etor?

00:37:57.368 --> 00:37:59.700
Tell them...

00:37:59.737 --> 00:38:02.399
they're on their own.

00:38:08.712 --> 00:38:12.671
They're changing course,
heading back to Romulan space.

00:38:12.716 --> 00:38:15.184
Make a full report
to the flagship

00:38:15.219 --> 00:38:17.517
take the main phasers off-line

00:38:17.554 --> 00:38:21.012
and begin radiation cleanup
of the affected decks.

00:38:21.058 --> 00:38:23.356
Yes, sir...

00:38:23.394 --> 00:38:25.225
Captain.

00:38:39.410 --> 00:38:40.934
Defeat.

00:38:41.011 --> 00:38:42.945
How?
Where are the Romulans?

00:38:43.013 --> 00:38:44.674
They never came.

00:38:52.923 --> 00:38:54.356
Kill him.

00:39:11.475 --> 00:39:13.136
No!

00:39:37.067 --> 00:39:39.035
Toral...

00:39:39.069 --> 00:39:41.936
the next leader of the Empire.

00:39:42.039 --> 00:39:46.135
Gowron is looking forward
to seeing you again.

00:39:49.546 --> 00:39:54.574
Captain's Personal Log,
Stardate 45025.4.

00:39:54.618 --> 00:39:56.483
It is with a profound
sense of relief

00:39:56.520 --> 00:39:59.717
that I have ordered the fleet
back to Federation territory

00:39:59.757 --> 00:40:01.748
following
the Romulan withdrawal

00:40:01.792 --> 00:40:03.953
and the news
of Gowron's victory.

00:40:04.061 --> 00:40:06.393
We have arrived
at the Klingon Homeworld

00:40:06.430 --> 00:40:08.193
where I will present
the High Council

00:40:08.232 --> 00:40:11.793
with a full report on our
encounter with the Romulans.

00:40:12.803 --> 00:40:13.792
Come.

00:40:16.440 --> 00:40:20.900
Captain, I wish to submit myself
for disciplinary action.

00:40:20.944 --> 00:40:23.970
I have disobeyed a direct order
from a superior officer.

00:40:24.014 --> 00:40:27.575
Although the result
of my actions proved positive

00:40:27.618 --> 00:40:29.586
the ends cannot justify
the means.

00:40:30.621 --> 00:40:32.111
No, they can't.

00:40:34.525 --> 00:40:38.689
However, the claim
"I was only following orders"

00:40:38.729 --> 00:40:43.928
has been used to justify too
many tragedies in our history.

00:40:43.967 --> 00:40:46.834
Starfleet doesn't want officers
who will blindly follow orders

00:40:46.870 --> 00:40:48.360
without analyzing the situation.

00:40:48.405 --> 00:40:52.603
Your actions were appropriate
for the circumstances

00:40:52.643 --> 00:40:55.077
and I have noted that
in your record.

00:40:57.414 --> 00:41:00.110
Mr. Data...

00:41:00.150 --> 00:41:03.449
nicely done.

00:41:03.487 --> 00:41:05.421
Sir.

00:41:18.936 --> 00:41:22.463
The Council appreciates
your report, Captain.

00:41:22.506 --> 00:41:25.942
The information
on the Romulan supply ships

00:41:25.976 --> 00:41:27.967
will prove very useful.

00:41:28.078 --> 00:41:30.842
Before you leave...

00:41:30.881 --> 00:41:36.183
there is one last matter
to attend to.

00:41:51.401 --> 00:41:52.868
Bring him.

00:42:00.577 --> 00:42:02.374
Toral

00:42:02.412 --> 00:42:04.380
son of Duras.

00:42:04.414 --> 00:42:07.872
You stand convicted of treason.

00:42:07.918 --> 00:42:11.877
The Duras family will one day
rule the Empire.

00:42:11.922 --> 00:42:15.551
Perhaps...

00:42:15.592 --> 00:42:18.390
but not today.

00:42:21.431 --> 00:42:22.659
Worf...

00:42:22.699 --> 00:42:28.729
this child's family
wrongly took your name

00:42:28.772 --> 00:42:32.731
and your honor from you.

00:42:32.776 --> 00:42:36.576
In return...

00:42:36.613 --> 00:42:42.176
I give his life... to you.

00:43:24.094 --> 00:43:26.392
What's wrong?

00:43:26.430 --> 00:43:28.898
Kill him!

00:43:28.932 --> 00:43:30.729
No.

00:43:30.767 --> 00:43:32.735
But it's our way.

00:43:32.769 --> 00:43:34.930
It's the Klingon way.

00:43:36.773 --> 00:43:40.072
I know...

00:43:40.110 --> 00:43:42.977
but it is not my way.

00:43:47.017 --> 00:43:48.780
This boy has done me no harm

00:43:48.819 --> 00:43:51.447
and I will not kill him
for the crimes of his family.

00:43:51.488 --> 00:43:53.046
Then it falls to Kurn.

00:43:55.959 --> 00:43:57.586
No!

00:43:57.628 --> 00:43:59.926
No, you gave me his life

00:43:59.963 --> 00:44:02.488
and I have spared it.

00:44:04.401 --> 00:44:06.631
As you wish.

00:44:16.580 --> 00:44:19.481
Request permission
to return to duty, sir.

00:44:21.318 --> 00:44:22.478
Granted.
